WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.165 --> 00:00:19.126
Mary walked down the path that led to the gate in the shrubbery.

2
00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:23.808
When she passed through the gate, she found herself in a big garden.

3
00:00:24.829 --> 00:00:26.690
There was a pool with an old fountain.

4
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.252
But the fountain was turned off, and the garden's flower beds were bare and wintry.

5
00:00:33.364 --> 00:00:36.265
Mary saw that the path came to an end at a brick wall.

6
00:00:38.886 --> 00:00:40.587
A green door in the wall stood open.

7
00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.649
She went through the door and came upon a new garden with walls all around it.

8
00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.611
She spied another open green door.

9
00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:54.613
Through that one she could see cold frames covering some of the garden beds.

10
00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:59.234
She seemed to be in the midst of a series of walled gardens.

11
00:01:00.795 --> 00:01:03.904
"This place is so bare and ugly," thought Mary.

12
00:01:03.924 --> 00:01:09.987
"It might be nicer in summer when things are green, but there is nothing pretty about it now."

13
00:01:11.587 --> 00:01:13.948
Soon an old gardener came through the door.

14
00:01:15.069 --> 00:01:19.731
He did not seem pleased to see her, but then again she was not pleased with his garden.

15
00:01:19.751 --> 00:01:22.272
"What is this place?"

16
00:01:22.772 --> 00:01:23.512
Mary asked.

17
00:01:23.532 --> 00:01:27.414
"One of the kitchen gardens, where we grow fruits and vegetables."

18
00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:29.575
"Can I walk through it?"

19
00:01:29.595 --> 00:01:32.736
"If you like, but there's nothing to see."

20
00:01:35.892 --> 00:01:40.514
Mary went through the second green door and saw that the cold frames were covering vegetables.

21
00:01:41.735 --> 00:01:45.496
In this garden was another green door, but it was closed.

22
00:01:45.516 --> 00:01:50.899
"I hope this is the secret garden," said Mary as she tried the handle.

23
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.221
But she opened the door quite easily and found herself in an orchard.

24
00:01:57.362 --> 00:01:59.383
It, too, was surrounded by a wall.

25
00:01:59.923 --> 00:02:01.504
Mary didn't see any more doors.

26
00:02:03.496 --> 00:02:08.660
She noticed the wall seemed to extend beyond the orchard, and she could see trees growing above the

27
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:14.484
wall. A bird with a bright red breast was sitting on the topmost branch of one tree.

28
00:02:15.705 --> 00:02:17.446
Suddenly he burst into song.

29
00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:21.669
It was as if he were calling to her.

30
00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:28.013
She stopped and listened, and somehow his cheerful, friendly song gave her a pleasant feeling.

31
00:02:29.174 --> 00:02:31.496
Even a disagreeable little girl may be lonely.

32
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:37.364
The big, closed house and big, bare moor had made Mary feel all alone in the world.

33
00:02:38.485 --> 00:02:43.169
But now the bird brought a look onto her sour face that was almost a smile.

34
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.492
She watched him until he flew off the branch.

35
00:02:46.512 --> 00:02:51.796
"I believe that tree is in the secret garden," she said.

36
00:02:52.997 --> 00:02:57.200
She walked back to the first kitchen garden and found the old man digging there.

37
00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.244
"I went into the orchard," said Mary.

38
00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:03.609
"There was no door into the next garden."

39
00:03:03.629 --> 00:03:06.051
"What garden?"

40
00:03:06.511 --> 00:03:08.112
the old man said sharply.

41
00:03:08.132 --> 00:03:10.914
"The one on the other side of the wall.

42
00:03:11.974 --> 00:03:14.676
A bird with a red breast was sitting in one of the trees."

43
00:03:15.896 --> 00:03:18.658
A slow smile spread over the old man's face.

44
00:03:18.678 --> 00:03:20.879
"That's the robin."

45
00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.562
He turned toward the orchard and whistled softly.

46
00:03:26.142 --> 00:03:28.424
The next moment a wonderful thing happened.

47
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.062
The bird flew toward them and landed near the gardener's foot.

48
00:03:33.082 --> 00:03:36.084
"Will he always come when you call him?"

49
00:03:36.604 --> 00:03:38.025
Mary asked in a whisper.

50
00:03:38.045 --> 00:03:41.847
"Yes. I've known him since he first tried to fly.

51
00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:45.889
When he flew over the wall, he was too weak to fly back.

52
00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:47.530
We got to be friends.

53
00:03:49.191 --> 00:03:53.594
Then when he finally flew back, he found the rest of his brood had left the nest.

54
00:03:54.635 --> 00:03:56.916
He was lonely, so he returned to me."

55
00:03:58.172 --> 00:04:00.153
Mary took a step closer to the robin.

56
00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.613
"I'm lonely."

57
00:04:01.633 --> 00:04:05.214
"I'm lonely too except when he's with me."

58
00:04:06.554 --> 00:04:08.075
The old man began to dig again.

59
00:04:08.095 --> 00:04:10.856
"He's the only friend I've got."

60
00:04:12.156 --> 00:04:12.976
"What's your name?"

61
00:04:13.496 --> 00:04:14.156
asked Mary.

62
00:04:14.176 --> 00:04:16.557
"Ben Weatherstaff.

63
00:04:17.057 --> 00:04:18.278
You and I are a bit alike.

64
00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:22.639
We're not good-looking, and we're both as sour as we look."

65
00:04:23.839 --> 00:04:26.560
Mary was surprised at the bold way Ben spoke to her.

66
00:04:27.676 --> 00:04:29.357
She wondered if what he said was true.

67
00:04:31.079 --> 00:04:34.461
Suddenly there was a clear rippling sound, and she turned around.

68
00:04:35.542 --> 00:04:39.685
The robin had flown into an apple tree and seemed to be singing right to her.

69
00:04:39.705 --> 00:04:43.669
"He's made up his mind to be friends with you," said Ben.

70
00:04:43.689 --> 00:04:46.210
"Would you make friends with me?"

71
00:04:46.731 --> 00:04:48.873
Mary asked the robin in a kind voice.

72
00:04:49.993 --> 00:04:51.194
The robin didn't answer.

73
00:04:51.655 --> 00:04:53.056
Instead he flew away.

74
00:04:55.596 --> 00:04:58.978
"He has flown into the garden with no door," said Mary.

75
00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.760
"He lives there.

76
00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:04.482
He's probably courting some lady robin who lives among the roses."

77
00:05:05.563 --> 00:05:06.984
"There are roses in that garden?"

78
00:05:08.004 --> 00:05:09.225
Ben began to dig again.

79
00:05:09.245 --> 00:05:11.947
"There were ten years ago," he mumbled.

80
00:05:11.967 --> 00:05:15.209
"I'd like to see them," said Mary.

81
00:05:15.229 --> 00:05:16.790
"Do you know of a door?"

82
00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.872
"There's none that anyone can find.

83
00:05:20.412 --> 00:05:23.034
Don't go looking for any doors," Ben warned her.

84
00:05:23.054 --> 00:05:25.476
"I must get on with my work now.

85
00:05:25.696 --> 00:05:26.478
Go on and play."

86
00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.467
And with that he threw his shovel over his shoulder and walked away.
